# RiskEngine Domain Rules

## Core Abstractions (never break these interfaces)

```
DecisionRequest  →  Engine.Evaluate()  →  DecisionResult
                         │
              ┌──────────┼──────────┐
         RuleEngine  ModelEngine  ListService
              └──────────┼──────────┘
                   FeatureService
```

## Decision Result Schema
Every `DecisionResult` MUST contain:
- `RequestID` string (UUID v4)
- `Decision` enum: PASS | REJECT | MANUAL_REVIEW
- `RiskScore` int (0–1000)
- `HitRules` []string
- `ModelScores` map[string]float64
- `RiskReasons` []string (reason codes, not free text)
- `CostMs` int64

## Rule Package Conventions
- One rule = one struct implementing `Rule` interface
- Rules are stateless; state lives in FeatureService
- Rule conditions use `pkg/expr` evaluator (never raw `eval`)
- Hot-reload via double-buffer + atomic pointer swap

## Feature Package Conventions
- `FeatureFetcher` interface: `Fetch(ctx, key) (FeatureMap, error)`
- Parallel fetch with 50ms total budget; per-fetcher timeout in config
- On timeout: log warn + use zero-value fallback (never block decision)
- Velocity features MUST use `pkg/sliding` window (Redis Lua atomic)

## Model Package Conventions
- Models loaded as ONNX via `pkg/onnx` wrapper (CGO pool-isolated)
- Model inference runs in dedicated goroutine pool (size = NumCPU)
- Champion-Challenger: traffic split via `orchestrator.ABRouter`

## Orchestrator Conventions
- Pipeline steps defined as DAG in YAML config; no hardcoded order
- Each step declares `timeout`, `parallel`, `onFailure` (SKIP|REJECT|FALLBACK)
- Result aggregation strategy configurable: HIGHEST_RISK | WEIGHTED | RULE_FIRST

## List Service Conventions
- L1: in-process Bloom filter (false-positive 0.1%)
- L2: Redis with TTL
- L3: persistent store (exact match)
- Query always starts at L1; short-circuit on miss

## Audit
- Every decision writes an `AuditRecord` to Kafka topic `risk.decisions`
- AuditRecord includes full feature snapshot + decision path
- Never log PII in plaintext; mask card numbers, phone numbers
